From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] USB disks for programs that write to them directly, and UAC for what asks for it.

Programs that write disks (Rufus first) now find what Windows has for them
(docs/disks.md): a USB disk the host does not use is a device of the setup
API and \\.\PhysicalDriveN, its partitions are volumes even with no file
system, the disk answers the partition table's requests, and volumes can be
locked, dismounted and given letters. A device can have a unix file
(wine_IoSetDeviceUnixPath): reads and writes go straight to it, requests stay
with the driver. Opening one to read or write it takes an elevated token.

A program whose manifest needs the administrator now asks through the
Application Information service before it is raised, as UAC does.

